  given a false pass.

  the bug

    * the release tarball unpacks to ytalexa/bin/cli.py, which
      is three levels below the extract root. The layout probe
      used find -maxdepth 2, so it matched nothing.
    * with find returning nothing, SRC became dirname "" which
      is ".", and the guard then tested ./bin/cli.py, a path
      relative to the current directory.
    * I had run my sandbox test from inside the repo, where
      ./bin/cli.py exists. So it passed by accident, reading my
      checkout instead of the download. On a phone the working
      directory is the home directory, there is no bin/cli.py,
      and it failed exactly as reported.
    * find -printf is a GNU extension as well, so that line was
      never safe on a busybox find either.

