0.4.0 - 2026-11-07
------------------

  first real Echo attempt. The tunnel worked on the first try.
  The skill did not run at all, and the reason was in the
  interaction model, not the server.

  what actually happened

    * the console transcript looked like a conversation. Say
      "सुरीली पेटी खोलो" under the old name and Alexa replied
      "आप क्या सुनना चाहते हैं?", then the song name drew an
      Amazon Music Unlimited advert.
    * both of those replies were Alexa's, not ours. The Test
      tab's JSON Input and JSON Output panels were empty and
      Skill Invocations listed nothing, which means the
      endpoint was never called once.
    * the old invocation name was "मेरा गाना", which means "my
      song". "अलेक्सा, मेरा गाना खोलो" parses as "open my
      song", so Alexa's built in music domain claimed it
      first. Amazon's naming rules say a name must not create
      confusion with existing Alexa features; two words is
      necessary but not sufficient, and I had only checked the
      word count.
    * the server was healthy the whole time. A POST to
      /alexa over the funnel returns the signature error it
      should, with server: ytalexa in the headers.

  fixed

    * invocation name is now "सुरीली पेटी", melodious box. It
      is deliberately not a word for song, music or radio, so
      nothing else wants the utterance.
    * check.sh now rejects an invocation name that is one word
      or that contains गाना, संगीत, music, song or radio. The
      rule that was only in my head is in CI now.

  second bug behind the first

    * even with the name fixed, the two turn flow could not
      have worked. AMAZON.SearchQuery only fills from an
      utterance that carries a carrier phrase, so a bare "लग
      जा गले" after the welcome prompt matches no sample and
      falls through.
    * the fix is Dialog.ElicitSlot. When the skill elicits the
      query slot by name, Alexa biases recognition toward that
      slot and the whole reply fills it, carrier phrase or
      not.
    * ElicitSlot errors unless the model carries a dialog
      section, and ours had none. Added dialog.intents for
      PlayIntent with elicitationRequired on query,
      delegationStrategy SKILL_RESPONSE so the handler stays
      in charge, and an Elicit.Slot.Query prompt.
    * every place that used to ask a question and wait now
      elicits instead: launch, help, fallback, empty slot, no
      search result, next or resume with an empty queue.
    * ax_rsp omits shouldEndSession when it is None, because a
      response carrying a Dialog directive must not pin the
      session either way. Callers that pass True or False are
      unchanged.

  checked by hand

    * the funnel endpoint answers over https with our server
      header, and rejects an unsigned POST
    * the elicit response has the directive, the slot stub and
      no shouldEndSession key, and no stale slot value
    * ax_rsp still emits shouldEndSession for ordinary replies
    * the model's elicitation prompt id resolves to a defined
      prompt with at least one variation
    * selftest is 93 assertions, up from 79
    * full check.sh passes

  known weak spots

    * ElicitSlot filling an AMAZON.SearchQuery slot from a
      bare utterance is behaviour Amazon's docs imply but
      never state outright. It is the standard workaround and
      I expect it to work, but this is the one part of this
      release I cannot prove from the documentation. If it
      misses, the one shot form with a carrier phrase is the
      guaranteed path and already works:
      "अलेक्सा, सुरीली पेटी से लग जा गले बजाओ".
    * nothing downstream of invocation is proven yet. No real
      Echo has fetched audio from this server, so the format,
      the signed url and the radio queue are all still
      untested against hardware.

  not done, on purpose

    * no en-IN interaction model. Adding one doubles what has
      to be rebuilt for every change and she speaks Hindi.
    * no name free invocation. It needs certification that a
      scraping skill will not get.


0.4.1 - 2026-11-07
------------------

  four bugs found by running this on a real device, in a proot
  Linux container rather than plain Termux. All four were mine.
  They had been patched locally on the device, which meant the
  next update would have erased them, so they are folded in
  here with tests.

  funnel mounted only one path

    * bin/tunnel.sh ran "tailscale funnel --set-path=/alexa"
      without --bg. That form runs in the foreground and
      serves until killed, so the script blocked there forever
      and the second call, the one that mounts /audio, never
      ran. The tunnel looked healthy because /alexa answered.
      Audio would have 404'd on the first song.
    * both calls take --bg now.

  stop left the server running

    * bin/run.sh writes its own pid to the pid file and then
      runs serve.py as a foreground child. SIGTERM to the
      supervisor is not delivered to that child while bash is
      waiting on it, so "ytalexa stop" reported success and
      the port stayed open.
    * run.sh now runs the child in the background, waits on
      it, and traps TERM, INT and HUP to kill it and leave.
    * cli stop signals the whole process group, then waits up
      to ten seconds for the port to actually close, then
      escalates to SIGKILL and says so. It only reports
      stopped once the port is really down.

  yt-dlp was eating the cookie jar

    * yt-dlp writes back whatever jar it is given, and it had
      already destroyed one component of the real cookie store
      on the device. It was being handed the master file.
    * ck_arg now copies the jar to a 0600
      ckrun-<videoid>.txt per download and gives yt-dlp the
      copy. au_tmp_clean removes it, so it goes on every exit
      path including timeout, spawn failure and success.
    * the two subprocess failure paths that did not clean up
      at all now do.

  the wizard could not see its own tunnel

    * tailscaled in a container runs userspace against a
      socket in $YTA_HOME, not the system one. st_tunnel
      called plain "tailscale funnel status", which talks to
      the system socket, so step 4 showed [ no ] while the
      funnel was up and serving.
    * all tailscale calls go through ts_cmd, which adds
      --socket when that file exists and falls back to the
      system socket if the private one answers nothing.

  while in there

    * four scripts had #!/data/data/com.termux/... hardcoded,
      which is not a path outside Termux. All four are
      /usr/bin/env bash now.
    * new command: ytalexa up. Starts tailscaled userspace if
      it is not answering, starts the server if the port is
      down, mounts the funnel if it is not mounted, prints
      status. Safe to re-run. A proot container has no
      Termux:Boot, so this is the recovery path after Android
      kills the container, and it is what a launcher button
      should call.
    * docs/SETUP-MOBILE.md has a section on container hosts:
      no boot hook, no wake lock, running as root, and the
      userspace tailscaled invocation.
    * SECURITY.md documents the cookie copy.

  checked by hand

    * both shell scripts parse
    * ck_arg returns a path that is not the master, 0600, with
      matching contents; clobbering the copy leaves the master
      valid; the copy is removed by the cleanup; a traversal
      tag cannot escape the directory
    * cli help lists up, version reports 0.4.1
    * selftest is 102 assertions, up from 93
    * full check.sh passes

  known weak spots

    * ytalexa up has no test. It needs tailscaled, a port and
      a funnel, none of which exist in CI. The pieces it calls
      are covered, the wiring is not.
    * the funnel --bg fix is reasoned from the symptom the
      device showed, not reproduced here, for the same reason.

  still unproven

    * no Echo has fetched audio from this server yet. The
      skill was never invoked in any test so far, so the audio
      format, the signed url and the radio queue remain
      untested against hardware.


