0.5.0 - 2026-11-07
------------------

  the Echo reached the skill, the skill did everything right,
  and Alexa threw the answer away. From his logs:

    03:58:40 search 'लग जा गले'
    03:58:42 radio -> 50 tracks
    03:58:49 audio  fetched APDPELjn9g8 3977 KiB in 7.1s
    03:58:49 alexa  play idx=0
    03:58:50 err alexa session error INVALID_RESPONSE

  nine seconds from request to reply. Alexa gives a skill
  eight. The INVALID_RESPONSE line only exists because 0.4.2
  started logging the error payload on SessionEndedRequest,
  which is the one piece of luck here.

  the mistake

    * ax_start called ax_fetch_at, which called au_get, which
      ran yt-dlp to completion before the response was built.
      Downloading four megabytes inside a request that has an
      eight second budget was never going to work. It passed
      in the simulator because the simulator has no deadline.
    * ax_do_play also built the radio queue inline, another
      two seconds, for tracks not needed until the first song
      is nearly over.
    * so the hard deadline was being spent on two things that
      did not need to be in the request at all.

  fixed

    * nothing downloads on the voice path now. ax_pick_at
      reads the queue entry and returns. The signed url goes
      back immediately; the bytes are fetched when the Echo
      asks for them, on the /audio route, which is an
      ordinary http fetch with no eight second rule.
    * ax_warm starts the current and next track in the
      background as soon as the reply is sent, so by the time
      the Echo follows the url the file is usually already
      there or well under way.
    * ax_fill builds the radio queue in the background and
      qu_extend appends it without disturbing idx or off.
      The first reply now carries the search results only,
      which is all that is needed to start playing.
    * measured here: search alone is 1.58s. That is the whole
      remaining request path, against a budget of 8.

  what was given up, and what replaced it

    * ax_fetch_at used to skip up to three unplayable videos
      by downloading each one to find out. That check cost
      the deadline, so it is gone.
    * instead PlaybackFailed now advances. ax_evt_skip reads
      the failing token, picks the next entry and returns a
      REPLACE_ALL for it. A dead video costs a hiccup rather
      than a download, and the Echo is the one that finds out
      it is dead, which is where that discovery belongs.

  so it cannot come back

    * check.sh parses alexa.py and walks the ast of every
      request path function: ax_start, ax_do_play, ax_do_step,
      ax_do_resume, ax_evt_near, ax_evt_skip, ax_intent,
      ax_route, ax_pick_at, ax_launch, ax_ask. If any of them
      references au_get, yr_radio, yr_merge or au_evict
      anywhere other than inside a nested background
      function, the build fails and says which one, and that
      alexa allows eight seconds.
    * ys_search is deliberately not on that list. It has to
      be in the request, it is the reason there is a reply at
      all, and at 1.6s it fits.

  checked by hand

    * qu_extend adds only new vids, keeps idx and off, keeps
      order, is idempotent, ignores junk rows and caps at
      QU_MAX
    * the guard catches a real regression: it failed first
      run and named ax_do_play
    * selftest is 128 assertions, up from 118
    * full check.sh passes

  still unproven

    * whether the Echo waits long enough on /audio for a
      cold track. If it does not, the next move is to stream
      the file as it downloads rather than after, which is a
      bigger change and is not worth making on a guess.


0.6.0 - 2026-11-07
------------------

  renamed again, and two real bugs behind "agla gana does not
  work properly". He reported three things: the rename, next
  and previous being unreliable, and Amazon Music stealing the
  speaker with no warning.

  * invocation name is now "अंश का बाजा", Ansh's music box. A
    personal name shares no word with Alexa's music domain, so
    unlike "मेरा गाना" it cannot be claimed before the skill is
    considered, and unlike "सुरीली पेटी" it is a name his mother
    already says every day. Docs, tests and the check guard
    follow the rename. The old names stay in this log because
    the log records what was true at the time.

  * BUG: the playing index never moved when the queue advanced
    by itself. AudioPlayer.PlaybackStarted only warmed the
    cache; it never wrote idx back to the state file, and a
    track that ends naturally sends PlaybackFinished, not
    PlaybackStopped, so nothing else wrote it either. After the
    first auto-advance, st["idx"] was still 0 while song two
    was audible. "अगला गाना" then computed 0+1 and replayed the
    song already playing, and "पिछला गाना" computed 0-1, clamped
    to 0, and also landed on something she had just heard.
    Exactly the "not working perfectly" he described. Both
    PlaybackStarted and PlaybackFinished now commit the index
    taken from the directive token, so idx is always the track
    the speaker is actually on.

  * BUG: "अगला गाना बजाओ" was being searched as a song. The
    built in playback intents carried no samples at all, so
    they relied entirely on Amazon's stock hi-IN utterances,
    while PlayIntent advertised "{query} बजाओ". The NLU matched
    the longer, more specific pattern and sent query="अगला गाना"
    to search. Next, Previous, Pause, Resume, Stop, Cancel,
    StartOver, Repeat and Help now carry explicit Hindi
    samples, and check.sh fails the build if the five playback
    ones lose them.

  * second line of defence for the same class of mistake:
    ax_ctl in src/alexa.py. If every word of an incoming
    PlayIntent query is either a filler word or a control word
    it is routed as the control instead of a search. Word lists
    are AX_FILL, AX_NEXT, AX_PREV, AX_HALT. The all-words rule
    is what keeps it safe: "बस इतना सा ख्वाब" still searches as a
    song even though "बस" alone means stop. Adding a word here
    needs no model rebuild.

  * Amazon Music cannot be disabled. It belongs to the account,
    not to a list of apps, and no setting removes it. Nor can
    the skill warn at the moment it takes over: a reply to an
    AudioPlayer event may not contain speech, and a skill
    cannot speak unprompted. So the warning had to move to the
    other side of the interruption.

    qu state gained two flags. "own" is set when the skill
    itself asks playback to stop, so an expected stop can be
    told apart from an unexpected one. On PlaybackStopped,
    stopped-without-own means cut=1, logged as "playback cut
    off at N ms". The next LaunchRequest sees cut=1, says
    "गाना बीच में रुक गया था। वहीं से आगे।" and resumes from the saved
    offset instead of asking what to play. One sentence and her
    place back, rather than silence. A deliberate "बंद करो"
    sets own first, so it does not trigger the notice.

  * ax_start takes a lead string so the notice can be spoken
    ahead of the track title in one response.

  * fixed a typo in the Hindi string for the end of the queue:
    "सूड़ी" was not a word. Now "गानों की सूची खत्म हो गई।".

  * docs/ALEXA-SKILL.md gained three sections: every phrase she
    can say, how to add a command and which of the two places
    to add it to, and what can and cannot be done about sharing
    the speaker with Amazon Music. SETUP.md gained the Routine
    recipe for a shorter trigger phrase. TEST.md Phase 5 gained
    the index checks, which are written to be run after letting
    the queue auto-advance, because that was the state the bug
    needed to show itself.

  * selftest 128 -> 153 assertions: t_control covers the phrase
    classifier in both scripts and the model samples, t_cut
    covers flag persistence and clearing.

  not done, on purpose: no attempt to grab the music domain
  back when Amazon Music wins an utterance. There is no API
  for it. Teaching her to include the invocation name is the
  only thing that works.
